WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:07.262
Zero Trust depends on visibility because access decisions are only as informed as the available signals.

00:00:07.262 --> 00:00:11.738
Organizations need useful information about identities, devices, applications, data, networks,

00:00:11.738 --> 00:00:13.976
policy actions, and security events.

00:00:13.976 --> 00:00:18.899
Monitoring begins before access with authentication, device, resource, and risk context.

00:00:18.899 --> 00:00:23.823
It continues during and after access through session events, application logs,

00:00:23.823 --> 00:00:27.851
policy decisions, administrative activity, and changes in security posture.

00:00:27.851 --> 00:00:31.880
Continuous evaluation allows policy to respond when conditions change.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:39.041
A request that was acceptable earlier may deserve additional verification or reduced access if risk increases,

00:00:39.041 --> 00:00:43.965
the device becomes noncompliant, or activity no longer matches expected use.

00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:46.203
Policy decisions should be observable.

00:00:46.203 --> 00:00:52.470
Logging which policy was evaluated, which signals were available, and why access was allowed,

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:57.841
limited, or denied helps operations teams troubleshoot problems and review security outcomes.

00:00:57.841 --> 00:00:59.184
Data quality matters.

00:00:59.184 --> 00:01:03.660
Missing logs, inconsistent identity fields, unsynchronized timestamps, unclear asset ownership,

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.345
and short retention can weaken analysis.

00:01:06.345 --> 00:01:10.374
Visibility programs should measure coverage and document known limitations.

00:01:10.374 --> 00:01:13.955
Analytics can help identify patterns and prioritize review,

00:01:13.955 --> 00:01:17.983
but automated risk scores should not become unexplained authority.

00:01:17.983 --> 00:01:21.116
Organizations need governance, testing, thresholds, human oversight,

00:01:21.116 --> 00:01:24.249
and a way to correct inaccurate decisions.

00:01:24.249 --> 00:01:26.487
Monitoring supports response and improvement.

00:01:26.487 --> 00:01:31.411
Security teams can investigate unusual access, identify policy gaps, tune controls,

00:01:31.411 --> 00:01:35.887
assist affected users, and feed lessons into identity, endpoint, application,

00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:37.230
and network programs.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:41.258
Visibility must be balanced with privacy and legal requirements.

00:01:41.258 --> 00:01:45.734
Collection should have a defined security purpose, appropriate access control,

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:48.420
retention limits, protection, and transparent governance.
